<!--
  Caste name prefixes.

  Six Colors carry a prefix between given name and family name, and each is the
  chemical symbol of the metal or element the caste is named for:

      Gold    au      Silver  ag      Copper  cu
      Blue    xe      Green   si      Gray    ti

  THE OMISSIONS ARE THE POINT, and they are deliberate rather than gaps:

    Red, Pink and Obsidian carry NO prefix, because the Society files them as
    property rather than as people. Leaving them plain is not an oversight, it is
    the same statement the prefix makes, in reverse.

    White, Yellow, Violet, Orange and Brown have no prefix in the reference either.
    They are left plain rather than given invented symbols - a fabricated caste
    marker would read as canon to anyone who did not know better, which is a worse
    outcome than an absence.

  The user is the authority on the setting and ruled on all of this directly.

  NAMES ARE ORIGINAL. No character name from the books appears here. The given
  names are ordinary historical Latin and Greek forms in the public domain, and the
  family names are built from syllables. Only the PREFIX CONVENTION is taken from
  the reference, and a convention is a rule, not an asset.

  Structure mirrored from Biotech/Defs/RulePackDefs/RulePacks_Namers_Xenohumans.xml
  (NamerPersonImpid), and the shared pools use RulePackDef.include, which vanilla
  uses the same way in Anomaly's RulePacks_Art.xml.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================= shared name material ======================== -->
  <!--
    Included by every namer below, so the pools are written once. The prefix is
    the only thing that differs between Colors.
  -->

